       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release (2,000 mg for extended-release). Single doses are usually no more than 850\u20131,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This order is double the maximum daily dose. That raises the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe intended order may have been 1700 mg total per day, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals. It may also have been 500 mg, 850 mg, or 1000 mg three times daily.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that. I'd add a note to the order that you verified the dose."
