       "text": "I entered the order as ORD-0001: metformin 1700 mg by mouth, three times daily with meals.\n\nThe order note says the 5,100 mg daily total is above the usual maximum. It also says you confirmed the dose is intentional and asks for pharmacy verification. Because the dose is so high, I'd watch the patient closely for GI intolerance and signs of lactic acidosis. Those signs include malaise, myalgias, respiratory distress, and abdominal pain. I'd also keep an eye on their renal function."
